WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:17.807
The moon was going down when Mowgli reached the wolves' cave.

2
00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:21.508
He was carrying Shere Khan's hide.

3
00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:27.998
"Mowgli?" Mother's eyes glowed.

4
00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:33.639
"We all knew you'd hunt Shere Khan one day. Well done!"

5
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.296
A deep voice came from some shrubs.

6
00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:42.317
"Well done indeed!" Bagheera ran toward them.

7
00:00:42.318 --> 00:00:50.487
"Mowgli, the jungle has been lonely without you."

8
00:00:50.488 --> 00:00:59.951
Soon the group of friends climbed up the hill to Council Rock.

9
00:00:59.952 --> 00:01:06.462
Mowgli spread the hide out on the flat stone at the top of Council Rock.

10
00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:17.660
As the wolves gathered, Mowgli beckoned Akela to lie on the hide.

11
00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:22.543
"Look well, oh, wolves!" Akela called loudly.

12
00:01:22.544 --> 00:01:26.541
The wolf pack had been without a leader for a while now.

13
00:01:26.542 --> 00:01:29.950
Many of the wolves were thin and hungry.

14
00:01:29.951 --> 00:01:32.458
Some were sick or wounded.

15
00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:36.922
Out of habit, they answered Akela's call.

16
00:01:36.923 --> 00:01:43.019
They stared in surprise when they saw the tiger's striped hide on the rock.

17
00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:50.103
A few gasped. "Shere Khan!" They looked toward Mowgli.

18
00:01:50.104 --> 00:01:55.001
"I have kept my word," the boy said proudly.

19
00:01:55.002 --> 00:01:58.795
A skinny wolf howled.

20
00:01:58.796 --> 00:02:01.767
"Please, Akela, lead our pack again.

21
00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:06.737
We are hungry and tired of living without laws."

22
00:02:06.738 --> 00:02:10.587
Bagheera grunted near Mowgli's ear.

23
00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:13.123
"This is what the wolves say now.

24
00:02:13.124 --> 00:02:18.049
When they are well-fed again, they will not listen to Akela or anyone."

25
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:24.222
Mowgli nodded. He didn't trust these wolves either.

26
00:02:24.223 --> 00:02:27.685
Later Mowgli returned to the cave.

27
00:02:27.686 --> 00:02:36.747
He slept for a day and a night, his heart feeling oddly heavy.

28
00:02:36.748 --> 00:02:40.154
When he awoke, Akela was visiting.

29
00:02:40.155 --> 00:02:42.850
So were Baloo and Bagheera.

30
00:02:42.851 --> 00:02:49.747
Everyone wanted to hear the story about the victory over Shere Khan again.

31
00:02:49.748 --> 00:02:55.274
"Akela and Gray Brother were a big help," Mowgli said.

32
00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:59.807
"You should have seen the buffalo pouring down the ravine!"

33
00:02:59.808 --> 00:03:04.240
"Well, I'm glad that I didn't see the humans throwing stones at you."

34
00:03:04.241 --> 00:03:08.547
Mother Wolf frowned. "I would have hunted all of them.

35
00:03:08.548 --> 00:03:15.398
Except for the kind woman who took care of you."

36
00:03:15.399 --> 00:03:19.158
"Calm down, Mother," Father Wolf said lazily.

37
00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:23.942
"Mowgli has come back again. What else matters?"

38
00:03:23.943 --> 00:03:27.614
Mowgli lay his head on Mother Wolf's side.

39
00:03:27.615 --> 00:03:34.996
"For my part, I never want to see or hear or smell humans again."

40
00:03:34.997 --> 00:03:38.409
Akela tilted his head to look at Mowgli.

41
00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:42.862
"What if the humans don't leave you alone, Little Brother?"

42
00:03:42.863 --> 00:03:45.920
Gray Brother growled softly.

43
00:03:45.921 --> 00:03:49.665
Bagheera twitched his tail and glanced at Akela.

44
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:53.235
"What made you say that?" he asked.

45
00:03:53.236 --> 00:03:59.392
"After last night's council, I went home along the trail," Akela answered.

46
00:03:59.393 --> 00:04:01.606
"I saw Mang the bat.

47
00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:07.062
He told me that the humans' village has been humming like a bees' nest."

48
00:04:07.063 --> 00:04:09.810
"So?" Mowgli shrugged.

49
00:04:09.811 --> 00:04:12.766
"The humans are often busy."

50
00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:18.243
"So, the bat saw the red flower blooming at the village gate.

51
00:04:18.244 --> 00:04:21.386
He also saw some men sitting near it.

52
00:04:21.387 --> 00:04:24.361
They were holding guns."

53
00:04:24.362 --> 00:04:27.312
Akela looked Mowgli in the eye.

54
00:04:27.313 --> 00:04:33.289
"And I believe I smelled a man along our trail this morning."

55
00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.077
"They are hunting you, Mowgli," Bagheera said.

56
00:04:37.078 --> 00:04:41.641
"But they threw me out of their pack!" Mowgli said.

57
00:04:41.642 --> 00:04:45.020
"Why can't they just leave me alone?"

58
00:04:45.021 --> 00:04:49.654
"You're a human, Little Brother," Akela replied softly.

59
00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:55.283
"We are animals. We cannot explain your kind to you."

60
00:04:55.284 --> 00:04:57.491
Mowgli looked down.

61
00:04:57.492 --> 00:05:00.336
He didn't know what to say.

62
00:05:00.337 --> 00:05:04.640
"What's that?" Bagheera sprang to his feet.

63
00:05:04.641 --> 00:05:08.759
He sniffed the air. His body stiffened.

64
00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:14.355
Gray Brother did the same thing, sniffing the wind that was blowing from the right.

65
00:05:14.356 --> 00:05:19.280
"It's a human's scent!" Bagheera said.
